        "note": "Bounded PR-1 plan for installing pinned Graft and wiring structural code-context for conductors and dispatched workers developing ops/. One shared stdlib module ops/devlane/harness/graft.py is the single reader of GRAFT_ENABLE/GRAFT_NODE/GRAFT_BIN and the single builder of every Graft invocation, consumed by the launcher over the allowed dispatch->harness edge and by a ops/bin/graft.sh lever for conductors; identity is frozen in a tracked pin.json (node v24.21.0 sha, Graft source rev 3a85a2f4, committed lockfile), disable is the one line GRAFT_ENABLE=0, cache is always outside snapshot/, refresh is disabled and update-check.json seeded so offline workers make no npm subprocess, and the external surface carries a contract, a native probe and a contract-verified fake. Five slices (graft-pin S, graft-config S, graft-surface M, graft-conductor S, graft-worker M) ordered by value per cost; graft-worker is the only slice that touches the dispatcher and lands last. Placement opinion (counts.opinions=1): the interface lives under ops/devlane/harness rather than ops/conductor/tools to avoid the instrument-conventions registry-closure gate the inventory forbids editing. Every unmeasured flag/behavior assumption is made a refusal (graft-unavailable/graft-residual/graft-readonly) and named against a decisive native probe (P-GRAFT-INSTALL/STRUCT/NONET/SNAPSHOT/WORKER) to run on a warmed host before graft-launch lands. Verified with which node/npm/graft (absent) and grep graft over lane.conf and launch.py (empty) at 20f9bcaf, so every named test is red for absence."
      }
