        "note": "Reds verified genuine: all four product suites fail on intended assertions reached through the bootstrap CLI/public seams (refusal-token, state, meta-dict, exit), no import/collection/ENOENT reds; green tests are the disabled->None/\"\" cases the stub satisfies. Fake protocol suite 15/15 green with no Node (node/bin/node is the fake script), confirming ordinary suites need neither Node nor network. Install-identity, provider-fault-with-transcript, freshness, descriptor-shape, adapter argument/tool validation, disabled byte-stability, withheld test-roles, ready-metadata+brief-digest, and end-to-end child-query witness all discriminate. Five findings: one P2 (resume/verify_worker custody proven only via descriptor digest; installation-pin, canonical-snapshot/relocation, and cache-location arms unexercised) and four P3 (default worktree cache isolation, probe disabled/unavailable conflation, provider-fault cache-residue unchecked, \"only install fetches\" proxy). Implementation is an intentional stub, so findings name the correct-shaped-but-wrong implementation each gap accepts rather than a planted mutant. Verdict changes. Report at out/SKEPTIC.md."
